No, it's still valid. The lifespan of the Candelabrum is initially
determined by the candles that are first placed into it (or added
afresh to a burnt-out Candelabrum); if candles are subsequently added
to it that have less remaining life than the Candelabrum, its lifespan
is reduced to that of the added candles. So if you particularly want
your Candelabrum to last as long as possible, make sure to only put
wax candles in it.

(And, of course, make sure only to light it on the invocation spot; each time
you light it anywhere else, its lifespan is halved.)

